      "writtenOn": "2021-02-12T03:14:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is not true. The call could be due to MSG_UPDATE_IFACES.\n\nThe intent of this null check was to ensure that only calling forceUpdateIfaces from ConnectivityService would update mDefaultNetworks. \n\nIt looks like there is a possible race here where MSG_UPDATE_IFACES sends a message with a stale copy of out-of-date mDefaultNetworks that CS is already updating. This is because the code for processing MSG_UPDATE_IFACES incorrectly reads mDefaultNetworks without grabbing the lock (and thus, the @GuardedBy annotation on mDefaultNetworks is incorrect).\n\nNot sure how to fix this. Can you file a bug to look at it?",
      "range": {
